{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408/events","html_url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408","id":6168736024,"node_id":"I_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABb69xGA","number":1408,"title":"Bug: carried MSM resource-cleanup patches write through an uninitialized pointer","user":{"login":"blitterbot","id":335883270,"node_id":"U_kgDOFAUsBg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/335883270?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot","html_url":"https://github.com/blitterbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7115394264,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABqBxM2A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-02T18:41:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T19:05:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found during T41 (#688), accepted Stage-B finding F-01 / L-01 and Stage-C punch item PL-001. **Severity: High. Owner: the base integration (#563/#559).** This is a source defect in the audited fork, not a report of an observed crash. The T41 lane makes no source fix.\n\n## Source trace\n\nAt audited source `02aab33bd9842610b0d466c9c186454dc14373ee` (unchanged from dispatch `d7dd766659`), both files contain the pre-fix version:\n\n- `projects/ROCKNIX/packages/linux/patches/7.0/0010-msm-resource-cleanup.patch`\n- `projects/ROCKNIX/packages/linux/patches/7.2/0010-msm-resource-cleanup.patch`\n\nThe first diff adds `cstate->num_mixers = 0;` at patch line 19; `cstate = to_dpu_crtc_state(crtc_state);` remains later, at patch line 37. In the **complete final SM8550 patched function**, the local pointer is declared at line 1441, written through at 1453 and first assigned at 1470. The full function has no earlier initialization; the global-state error return does not initialize the successful path. SM8550's configuration enables `CONFIG_DRM_MSM=y` at line 4461. H700 and GENERIC_X64 do not enable that driver in the configurations read. Both carried patch copies are byte-identical.\n\nExpected: initialize the local pointer before its first dereference. Actual: the first field write precedes initialization. This permits an indeterminate-pointer write on an enabled MSM DPU path. The accepted normal applications all succeed; application success does not establish code correctness.\n\n[Complete final function and numbered trace](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/7e5d1546712df2eb79c585fce663186770d1ceb9/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-shipped-kernel/stage-b/corrected/0010-final-function.txt), [accepted refutation](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/7e5d1546712df2eb79c585fce663186770d1ceb9/docs/audits/2026_11_02-epic-m6-patches-shipped-kernel/04-analysis.md#finding-verification-phase-45).\n\n## Existing upstream fix\n\n[9416eec2c200ad969d9e421e686fc7cbfdaca36a](https://github.com/ROCKNIX/distribution/commit/9416eec2c200ad969d9e421e686fc7cbfdaca36a), `kernel: msm dp resource cleanup patch fix uninit pointer`, states:\n\n> Previous version writes to field pointed by an uninitialized pointer.\n\nThe immutable local history shows the fix moves initialization before the write in both copies. The retained two-path comparison of the audited source against pinned upstream `651150fc88` reports:\n\n```text\n2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)\n```\n\nRoute uptake through the existing base integration; do not repair these carried patches on the T41 audit branch. No upstream submission is needed for an already-fixed upstream defect.\n\n**Already written:** H700, SM8550 and GENERIC_X64 image builds using the fork's pre-fix source since the base consume these pre-fix patch bytes; this audit did not inspect built images or installed devices. Only SM8550's enabled affected driver is established by the configurations read. The base merge corrects future source/builds; installed images remain unchanged until their normal update. No storage schema, migration or cloud write is introduced by this source correction, and no existing device state was read or changed by this audit.\n\n**Can this be done on the VM?** No — the tree, history and accepted final touched-source artifact establish this source defect; nothing a guest shows is a provenance fact. Build, guest and physical-runtime qualification remain outside this source-only lane. No runtime occurrence or runtime fix is claimed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The base integration records `fixed-at` and the contemporaneous `upstream/next` commit; after the merge, `git diff --stat <fixed-at> upstream/next -- projects/ROCKNIX/packages/linux/patches/7.0/0010-msm-resource-cleanup.patch projects/ROCKNIX/packages/linux/patches/7.2/0010-msm-resource-cleanup.patch` is empty, with the two hashes and command output retained.\n- [ ] A source trace for both corrected siblings places `cstate = to_dpu_crtc_state(crtc_state)` before the first `cstate->num_mixers` write and cites the integration commit carrying upstream `9416eec2c200ad969d9e421e686fc7cbfdaca36a`; the issue retains this Already written/VM account and `tools/box-check --issue <this issue>` reports 0 fail.\n\nFiled by Codex / GPT-6-Astra / xhigh, T3 `m6-t3-emulators`, session `01a19d12-29e3-7fe0-9f41-038dac0a5deb`; identity observed in the live Herdr footer, not provider-attested. Reactive bug: no milestone or parent.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1408/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/r